/T (ISSP attacked Niamey's international airport, the symbolic seat of the Alliance of Sahel States, on 29 January. In February, JNIM launched its largest offensive in Burkina Faso, the subsequent ISSP counter-offensive revealed intensified intra-jihadist competition for territory and revenue. Successful and failed coup attempts in Guinea-Bissau and Benin respectively suggest political instability could spread towards anglophone West Africa. In the South and East, Zimbabwe moved to scrap direct presidential elections and extend President Mnangagwa's term to 2030, while Uganda's President Museveni secured a seventh term. )
/E (ISSP attacked Niamey's international airport, the symbolic seat of the Alliance of Sahel States, on 29 January. In February, JNIM launched its largest offensive in Burkina Faso, the subsequent ISSP counter-offensive revealed intensified intra-jihadist competition for territory and revenue. Successful and failed coup attempts in Guinea-Bissau and Benin respectively suggest political instability could spread towards anglophone West Africa. In the South and East, Zimbabwe moved to scrap direct presidential elections and extend President Mnangagwa's term to 2030, while Uganda's President Museveni secured a seventh term. )
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [1001 0 R 4 1002 0 R 6 1003 0 R 8]
