/T (The Czech Republic warns that the MFF risks increasing administrative complexity. It argues that, because underdeveloped regions are more likely to lack administrative capacity, a central fund risks widening disparities as more developed regions enjoy proportionally greater access to investment. This suggests that, despite increased funding availability, investment outcomes may remain uneven across the region. )
/E (The Czech Republic warns that the MFF risks increasing administrative complexity. It argues that, because underdeveloped regions are more likely to lack administrative capacity, a central fund risks widening disparities as more developed regions enjoy proportionally greater access to investment. This suggests that, despite increased funding availability, investment outcomes may remain uneven across the region. )
