/E (Global economic volatility in Q1 2026 was driven by the interaction between energy availability, corridor reliability, and financing ability. Economies with stronger fiscal buffers, rerouting capacity, and policy-backed sectors should remain investable even under stress, while energy-importing and externally financed economies will stay more exposed. Our base case is for slower but still selective cross-border activity in Q2. The upside case depends on the rate of de-escalation in the Middle East and our downside case is a longer shock cycle in which economic disruptions intensify with no viable off-ramps for conflicting parties.)
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
