/Title (North America remained a leading force of economic power in Q1 of 2026, with significant focus on bolstering security and resilience through greater prioritisation of regional trade and domestic manufacturing. Key economic strategies including significant deregulation, market diversification, and efforts to boost domestic industries shaped this quarter. Structural changes across the US, Canada, and Mexico suggest potential for increased investment in sectors such as energy, technology, auto, and agriculture. However, the Middle East conflict has caused significant instability in oil and energy markets, creating supply shortfalls and price spikes that pose short and long-term risks for regional fiscal security.)
